  },
  "description": "Brake (hold back) before the drops. The SLOW signs mark each descent and the ! marks the lip. The small step on the first hill is a warm-up with a long, flat runout. The apple waiting at the foot of each drop is only caught by rolling off it slowly, so a rider who flies off sails over it. The last descent is long and fast: brake hard before the lip, roll down onto the landing for the apple, and stop before the tyre wall at the end of the lane.",
